ignment is safe."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Reducer Weight","type":"heading","anchor":"Reducer-Weight","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}]},{"text":"Effect Threading","type":"heading","anchor":"Effect-Threading","level":2},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"text":". Blocking calls (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "